    {
      "input": "Thanks *he said to them, after which he decides to give them back the boots*\nYou'll need them more than me",
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Nicco speaks his thanks, then offers the boots back to Korvin, saying he'll need them more.\n\nKorvin's small, mobile eyes flick from Nicco's face to the boots and back. He makes no move to take them. \"Boots are boots,\" he says, his voice gruff and practical. \"You bought 'em. I sold 'em. Transaction's done.\" His large, damaged hands stay at his sides, one thumb worrying at a callus on the other palm. \"Wear 'em, sell 'em, give 'em to the next beggar—none of my concern now.\" He gives Nicco a long, perceptive look, something cautious in his bearing, though his expression doesn't shift much. \"You standing out here handing back goods to every trader you meet, or am I special?\"",
